<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"className":"hk-title__sub"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading hk-title__sub">Questions before you enrol</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-intro"} -->
<p class="hk-intro">Find clear, factual answers regarding the Hakari Course curriculum, kit delivery, online examination, fees, and refund policies.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:group {"className":"hk-read hk-read--faq","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group hk-read hk-read--faq"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3,"className":"hk-rh hk-rh--grp"} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading hk-rh hk-rh--grp">Course</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:group {"className":"hk-weeks","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group hk-weeks"><!-- wp:details {"className":"hk-week hk-faqrow"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details hk-week hk-faqrow"><summary>Do I need prior food hygiene qualifications to enrol?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">No prior formal certifications or hygiene diplomas are required to join the course. The Hakari Course is designed specifically for working adults who supervise or will soon supervise food preparation—including shift leads, sous-chefs, baker leads, and food-truck owners. The syllabus begins with foundational biological, chemical, physical, and allergen hazards before progressing to advanced Codex Alimentarius HACCP principles and shift leadership. All that is required is active access to a commercial kitchen, bakery, or catering facility where you can complete your five practical probe checks.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"className":"hk-week hk-faqrow"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details hk-week hk-faqrow"><summary>Which countries is this supervisor course suitable for?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">The course content is built directly on the internationally recognized seven HACCP principles established by the Codex Alimentarius General Principles of Food Hygiene. Because these core hygiene rules underpin food safety legislation worldwide—including European, British, and international standards—the practical controls taught are applicable in any commercial kitchen environment. We focus on objective culinary physics and biological science, such as keeping hot food at or above 63 °C, ensuring core cooking reaches 75 °C, and chilling below 5 °C, making the supervisory skills universally relevant across borders.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"className":"hk-week hk-faqrow"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details hk-week hk-faqrow"><summary>What equipment is included in the practical training kit?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">The practical kit included in the €390 course fee provides essential tools to complete your hands-on kitchen temperature checks. It contains a professional digital probe thermometer with rapid readout, a specialized calibration cup for testing probe accuracy in iced water, a dispenser of 50 disinfectant probe wipes, a printed temperature log pad, and a pencil. The kit ships within 5 working days of completed enrolment to ensure it arrives before your practical assignments commence. Learners who already possess appropriate equipment can choose the course without kit option for €340.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"className":"hk-week hk-faqrow"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details hk-week hk-faqrow"><summary>How much study time should I budget each week?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">The course requires approximately three hours of study per week across the six-week schedule, totaling around 18 hours of combined learning. Each week features four concise video lessons lasting 10 to 20 minutes each, allowing you to learn during quiet prep periods or after service. In addition, learners are encouraged to attend the live one-hour Q&amp;A session held every Tuesday from 18:30 to 19:30 CET, or watch the recorded replay if working service. Completing your five practical kitchen probe checks requires roughly 15 minutes of hands-on logging per week.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:heading {"level":3,"className":"hk-rh hk-rh--grp"} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading hk-rh hk-rh--grp">Exam and certificate</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:group {"className":"hk-weeks","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group hk-weeks"><!-- wp:details {"className":"hk-week hk-faqrow"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details hk-week hk-faqrow"><summary>How is the final online examination proctored?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">The final exam is conducted entirely online using secure proctoring software accessible from your web browser. You will need a computer or laptop equipped with a functional webcam, microphone, and stable internet connection. The examination contains 40 multiple-choice questions focusing on supervisor scenarios, critical limits, hazard analysis, and corrective actions. You have 60 minutes to complete the test under quiet conditions. The proctoring system verifies candidate identity and confirms that the assessment is completed independently without external notes or reference books.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"className":"hk-week hk-faqrow"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details hk-week hk-faqrow"><summary>What happens if I do not pass the exam on my first try?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">If you do not achieve the required 75 % pass mark on your initial attempt, there is no need to worry. Every standard enrolment includes one free exam resit, which can be scheduled at any convenient time within 30 days of your first attempt. Your tutor will highlight the specific syllabus modules where knowledge gaps appeared, allowing you to review the lesson videos and log materials before sitting the assessment again. Should a learner require further attempts beyond this free resit, an extra exam resit costs €60.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"className":"hk-week hk-faqrow"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details hk-week hk-faqrow"><summary>How quickly is my supervisor certificate issued and how long is it valid?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">Once you have successfully passed the online proctored exam with a score of 75 % or higher, your official Hakari Course certificate is generated as a secure digital PDF and issued within 2 working days. The certificate validates that you have completed comprehensive training in Codex Alimentarius HACCP principles and practical food-safety supervision. The certificate remains valid for 3 years from its date of issuance. If you ever require a replacement copy or an official second-language version, re-issuance is available for an administrative fee of €20.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:heading {"level":3,"className":"hk-rh hk-rh--grp"} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading hk-rh hk-rh--grp">Payment and refunds</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:group {"className":"hk-weeks","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group hk-weeks"><!-- wp:details {"className":"hk-week hk-faqrow"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details hk-week hk-faqrow"><summary>What is your refund policy if my schedule changes?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">We offer clear and transparent cancellation terms to give working supervisors flexibility. If you need to cancel your enrolment before your cohort begins, you are entitled to a 100 % full refund up to 14 days before the official start date. Once the cohort has commenced, you may still request a full refund within the first 14 days of the course, provided you have opened fewer than 25 % of the available online lessons. All refund requests should be directed to our support desk for prompt resolution.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"className":"hk-week hk-faqrow"} -->
<details class="wp-block-details hk-week hk-faqrow"><summary>Can businesses enrol multiple team members together?</summary><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-body"} -->
<p class="hk-body">Yes, we frequently train entire supervisory teams from restaurants, bakeries, school catering services, and food manufacturing sites. For businesses registering five or more learners from the same company within a single cohort, we offer a discounted team seat rate of €330 per person, which includes individual practical testing kits dispatched directly to your business address. Tomás Brandt coordinates corporate registrations and can issue formal company invoices including VAT upon request. Invoices can be settled by bank transfer before the cohort commencement date.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>
<!-- /wp:details --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --></div>
<!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"hk-textlink hk-textlink--c"} -->
<p class="hk-textlink hk-textlink--c">Still have a question? <a href="/contact/">Write to us</a>; we reply within one working day.</p>
